-- R14 — One direction per underlying: never long and short the same underlying at once; a replacement card fills only after
-- the old card's exit bar has closed. Tightens R08 for the same underlying (R08's cross-proxy tests and NET line stay).
-- Owner request, 30 Oct 2026 (project chat, "I thought we agreed not to have long and short trades of same thing at same time";
-- thread "Opposite-side trade conflict rule"): the Opus digest of 30 Oct closed P03 short EURUSD under R08 at the 09:00 SGT bar
-- close while its replacement P19 long EURUSD filled at that bar's open, and R08 2(ii) would still have allowed an opposite
-- tactical in another contract month of the same commodity (Jan-27 vs Feb-27 Brent).
-- Proposed 30 Oct 2026 from a cloud thread with this exact statement (dash.propose_rule raises no approval prompt);
-- apply_after = the next Sunday 20:00 SGT window (Sun 1 Nov 2026), when the Sunday "apply rules" task puts it in force unless
-- the owner replies "oppose R14" to the weekly review email; both digests then read it through dash.rules_in_force() from the
-- Mon 2 Nov 07:15 SGT run. Rerunning this file would propose a new rule id, so run it only to re-propose after a revert.
-- To put it in force before the Sunday window (one line in the Supabase SQL editor, project diiwqbxyhtgvozhncoef):
--   update dash.rules set status = 'in_force', decided_at = now(), apply_after = now() where rid = 'R14' and status = 'proposed';
select dash.propose_rule($j${"scope": "both", "title": "One direction per underlying: never long and short the same underlying at once; a replacement card fills only after the old card's exit bar has closed", "body": "ONE DIRECTION PER UNDERLYING (owner, 30 Oct 2026). Tightens R08 for the same underlying; where the two differ, this rule applies. R08's CONFLICT review, its cross-proxy tests (the same factor label with the opposite sign, or a correlation at or beyond 0.7 between DIFFERENT underlyings) and its NET line for those cross-proxy pairs are unchanged.\n\n1. SAME UNDERLYING means: the same proxy; the same instrument in another wrapper (NQZ26 / ^NDX / QQQ; ^KS11 / EWY; GCZ26 / GLD; a spot cross and its forward or NDF); the same commodity, index, bond or pair in another contract month or tenor (Jan-27 and Feb-27 Brent; ZNZ26 and ZNH27; a 1W and a 1M forward of one pair). A calendar, curve, crack or ratio spread carded explicitly as a spread with both legs named (BZG27-BZZ27, ^TYX-^FVX, HOF27/CLF27) is its own underlying: it is not matched against an outright in one of its legs, and two spreads are the same underlying only when their legs match.\n\n2. THE RULE. The book never holds a long and a short of the same underlying at the same time, open or pending, in any class (thematic, tactical, hedge). R08 item 2(ii), which let an intact card stay beside an opposite tactical or hedge with a NET line, no longer applies to the same underlying. An opposite lean in the same underlying has two outcomes only: (a) the R08 review finds the open card dead, or weakened by the new lean's own evidence: close it (VIEW CHANGED, FIRST-HOUR EXIT; a pending card is vetoed) and card the replacement only if it passes THE TRADE TEST on its own numbers; (b) the open card is intact: TESTED records the lean as \"not carded (f): opposite to open Pnn - thesis intact, one direction per underlying\" and the open card's REVIEW line gains the opposing evidence. Horizon, class, contract month and \"the tactical names its exit\" are never reasons to hold both.\n\n3. REPLACEMENT FILL. A replacement card never fills while the card it replaces is open. Its fill is the open of the first hourly bar of the proxy that starts after the old card's exit bar has closed: fill = the later of its usual fill (the first hourly bar after its opened time) and the bar after the old card's FIRST-HOUR EXIT bar. Decision at 08:15 SGT: the old card exits at the close of the 09:00 bar (10:00 SGT) and the replacement fills at the open of the 10:00 bar, not the 09:00 bar. The card prints \"fills <HH:MM SGT> (after Pnn exits at the <HH:MM> bar close)\". REF, stop, target, r/r, EV and the gate are unchanged; NO-CHASE and VOID are measured from the actual fill as usual. If the old card's exit bar has not printed by the next run (weekend, holiday, no hourly bars), the replacement stays pending until it has, and its row says so. The same ordering applies when a reader's \"close Pnn\" or \"veto Pnn\" and a pending opposite card coincide, and to a re-entry after a stop on the same underlying while a card the other way is still open.\n\n4. PRINT. The BOOK line never shows one underlying with both signs. While a replacement waits behind a closing card, the two rows read \"closing - first hour after <HH:MM SGT> (R08)\" and \"fills after Pnn exits\"; a NET line is printed only for cross-proxy pairs under R08 and never for the same underlying.\n\n5. FIRST RUN under this rule, both books: if the book holds a long and a short of the same underlying, open or pending, apply item 2 at once (review, close the weaker by FIRST-HOUR EXIT or veto the pending card) and log it; a spread card and an outright in one of its legs are not a pair.", "rationale": "Owner, 30 Oct 2026: \"I thought we agreed not to have long and short trades of same thing at same time\". R08 still allowed an intact card beside an opposite tactical or hedge, and the one-hour gap between a first-hour exit (a bar's close) and the replacement's fill (the same bar's open) left the book both ways in one underlying.", "evidence": "Opus 30 Oct 2026: P03 short EURUSD closed under R08 (CONFLICT weakened, view changed at 08:15 SGT, exit at the 09:00 bar close) while its replacement P19 long EURUSD was set to fill at the 09:00 bar open, so the book held both for one hour; the same run's CONFLICT line kept P15 short Feb-27 Brent as intact against a long Jan-27 Brent lean (not carded under R08 because it was thematic; a tactical in the other month would have been allowed). Fable 22 Oct: P23 long NQZ26 (tactical) carded against P13 short NQZ26, both held for a session.", "revert_if": "Revert if, over 4 weeks, a weekly review finds 3 or more leans refused under item 2(b) that would have earned 1R or more while the kept card lost, or the replacement-fill delay under item 3 costing more than 0.3R on average over 5 or more replacements (fill versus the bar it would otherwise have filled), or the owner asks for the tactical overlay back.", "supersedes": null, "review_due": "2026-12-11", "source": "owner"}$j$::jsonb);
